rain-core: xray/0049-muxcool-downlink-backpressure
Source: ReClash fix on top of xray/0037 (GPL-3.0).

The carrier read loop feeds every session on one physical connection. A TCP
consumer that stopped reading filled the 16-frame channel and blocked that
loop, stalling all sibling sessions. Replace the channel with a byte- and
frame-bounded queue that producers never block on: a session whose consumer
falls 256 KiB behind is reset with ErrSessionOverflow (the caller sees the
error; TCP data is never silently dropped or reordered), and the carrier
keeps serving the others. UDP keeps lossy datagram semantics with its own
byte cap and a drop counter. A carrier-wide budget bounds the sum of queued
payload, and the queue returns pooled buffers on overflow, reset and close.
Session End is now sent from a goroutine so a stalled carrier cannot hold
Close or the read loop.

Tests: TestSlowStreamConsumerDoesNotBlockSibling,
TestCarrierDownlinkBudgetResetsOnlyThePushingSession,
TestPacketSessionDeliversQueuedDatagramsBeforeRemoteEnd,
TestPacketSessionExpiredDeadlineWinsOverQueuedData,
TestByteQueueReleasesDroppedAndSealedItems, TestByteQueueDrainsSealedItemsBeforeClosing,
TestPacketSessionFullQueueDoesNotBlockOtherSessions.

